Description: avfilter/tonemap: apply the RPU's linear matrix to LMS before LMS to RGB
 For Dolby Vision reshaping, the tone-map filters convert linear LMS to
 RGB with the product of two matrices: the RPU's rgb_to_lms matrix
 (dovi->linear; for profile 5 the inverse of the 2 % crosstalk matrix)
 and the constant LMS to BT.2020 RGB matrix. The definition, and
 libplacebo, apply the RPU's matrix to LMS first. The filters built the
 product as ff_matrix_mul_3x3(dst, dovi_lms2rgb_matrix, linear), which
 is linear x dovi_lms2rgb_matrix, so LMS to RGB acted first and the
 crosstalk inverse was applied to RGB. BT.2100 table 7 fixes the order
 too: the inverse of its ICtCp RGB to LMS matrix equals the LMS to RGB
 matrix times the inverse of its 4 % crosstalk matrix.
 .
 The rows of both matrices sum to one, so greys came out right and the
 error grew with saturation. On flat profile 5 patches converted to
 BT.2020 PQ, colours 140 to 260 base-layer codes from neutral came out
 0.7 to 2.2 luma codes off on average, up to 13 luma and 22 chroma
 codes. tonemapx and tonemap_cuda carried the same error, so they
 agreed with each other but not with the definition.
 .
 Multiply in the right order in tonemapx, tonemap_cuda, tonemap_opencl,
 tonemap_videotoolbox and tonemap_d3d11. Input without Dolby Vision
 reshaping does not reach this product.
Author: Streamarr
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-11
